# .env is the security-critical exclusion here, not a housekeeping one.
# Docker image layers are immutable and additive -- if .env were COPYed
# into an early layer and then "deleted" in a later one, the API key
# would STILL be recoverable from the image's layer history (`docker
# history`, or just `docker save` + inspect the tarball) -- deleting a
# file in a later layer only hides it from the final filesystem VIEW, it
# does not remove it from the earlier layer's contents. The only correct
# fix is never COPYing it into any layer in the first place. The real key
# gets injected at `docker run -e GOOGLE_API_KEY=...` or
# `--env-file .env` instead -- both are pure runtime mechanisms, entirely
# separate from the image build, so the secret never touches a layer.
.env

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Test code and docs don't belong in a production image -- smaller
# image, and no reason to ship internal learning notes to whatever
# registry this eventually gets pushed to.
tests/
*.md
